<title>JAPAN: McDonald's launches 30 bln yen/$ Samurai.</title>
<headline>McDonald's launches 30 bln yen/$ Samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald's Corp launched 30 billion yen worth of 5.0 percent dual-currency samurai bonds due May 16, 2000, market sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The issue was priced at par and the coupon will be paid on May 16 annually.</p>
<p>The subscription period runs from October 31 to November 18 and the payment is due on November 19, they said.</p>
<p>McDonald's has ratings of Aa2 from Moody's Investor Service and AA from Standard and Poors.</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk 813-3432-8676</p>
</text>
